== check esc.salam --no-color
error[E001]: unknown identifier 'oops'
 --> esc.salam:2:31
2 |     println "\x1b]0;title\x07<U+0085>\x7fx" + oops
  |                                               ^
  = help: 'oops' is not defined in function 'main' and not defined globally.
     No import or include provides it either.
     If you forgot to define it, write 'oops := value' before this line.
exit 1
== check bidi.salam --no-color
error: invisible Unicode bidirectional control character U+202E in code: it can make the code look different from what it compiles to
 --> bidi.salam:2:6
2 |     a<U+202E>b := 1
  |      ^^^^^^^^
  = help: delete it: outside strings and comments it only hides what the code really is
error: invisible Unicode bidirectional control character U+2066 in code: it can make the code look different from what it compiles to
 --> bidi.salam:3:14
3 |     println a<U+2066>b
  |              ^^^^^^^^
  = help: delete it: outside strings and comments it only hides what the code really is
error[E001]: unknown identifier 'a<U+2066>b'; did you mean 'a<U+202E>b'?
 --> bidi.salam:3:13
3 |     println a<U+2066>b
  |             ^
  = help: If this is not a spelling mistake:
     'a<U+2066>b' is not defined in function 'main' and not defined globally.
     No import or include provides it either.
     If you forgot to define it, write 'a<U+2066>b := value' before this line.
  = fix: Change to 'a<U+202E>b'
error[E059]: unused variable 'a<U+202E>b': nothing uses it after it is declared; remove the declaration, or use the value where it was meant to be used; starting the name with '_' hides this error but is not advised, since the dead code stays in the program
 --> bidi.salam:2:5
2 |     a<U+202E>b := 1
  |     ^
  = fix: Prefix the name with '_'
exit 1
